# Cloudflare static-asset headers (applied by Workers Assets; ignored by `next dev`).
# Next.js static export cannot use CSP nonces, so inline scripts and styles are
# allowed. Third-party origins are Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics, both
# gated behind consent. Adding an analytics tool means adding its origins here
# too, or the browser silently blocks it — `next dev` ignores this file, so a
# missing origin only shows up in production.
#
# c.bing.com is deliberately absent from img-src. Clarity's loader fires an
# unconditional pixel at c.clarity.ms/c.gif that redirects to c.bing.com —
# Microsoft Advertising identity sync, the _uetmsclkid/_uetvid cookies. It is
# hardcoded in the tag, runs before the project config is read, and no Clarity
# setting disables it, so blocking the redirect here is the only lever. Nothing
# is lost: recordings, heatmaps and metrics are unaffected, and it keeps the
# site to the analytics-only promise the consent banner makes. The cost is one
# CSP violation logged per page load — that message is the block working, not a
# bug. Do not add c.bing.com to img-src to silence it.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.clarity.ms https://*.clarity.ms https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.clarity.ms https://c.bing.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.clarity.ms https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
